<title>UK: British Energy invests in gas power station - FT.</title>
<headline>British Energy invests in gas power station - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Energy Plc is set to announce investment in its first gas-fired power station, the Financial Times reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The joint announcement with French energy group Elf is expected to involve Humber Power, a power station in Humberside, northeast England, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>British Energy confirmed it had been in discussions with Elf and said its expansion plans could include &quot;entering into partnerships where appropriate&quot;, according to the FT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7717</p>
